WEBVTT

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.440
Damn, that's small!

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.780
Hey, I thought this was supposed to 
be comparable to Urayasu's castle.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.690
I guess they didn't want 
to make it too big.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:43.590
But isn't this the imperial capital?

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.950
It's an empire. This is supposed 
to be St. Chihiro's capital!

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.980
It's the St. Piria empire.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:49.960
And that's the emperor's castle?

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.700
The Princess Ecarlate and 
her retinue have arrived!

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.570
It really is small!

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:02.470
What the hell is this?

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:06.980
Is it maybe underground? 
Like some kind of underground empire?

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.690
What kind of nonsense 
are you spouting now?

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:11.790
Depart!

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.520
What's going on?

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.200
Did the castle just move?

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.330
It's one way to use Alma technology.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.330
The capital is too spread out.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:33.720
I don't even know how long it would 
take if you traveled conventionally.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.620
Let's spend the night in this castle.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.590
By tomorrow morning, we'll be at 
the entrance to the royal castle.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.210
Wow, the capital is amazing.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:01.610
Who now?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.920
Lord Nabokov Jugglaburk, my Liege.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:14.000
Yes, yes, and Lord Jugglaburk, 
you came here for what, exactly?

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.640
To talk about my betrothed.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.260
And who was that again?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.260
The 36th queen's descendant, 
Princess Ecarlate.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:29.270
Oh right, oh right, so you 
are to be my son-in-law?

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:33.690
However, I have heard that the 
princess has gone missing.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:35.270
Has she now?

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.280
I have also heard rumors 
that she has been murdered.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.280
Who has said such a thing?

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.350
Information always leaks.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:46.780
Who leaked it?!

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.540
Not me.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.040
They came from me.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.040
I beg your pardon?

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.660
My Liege, if you will come this way.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.050
Lord Jugglaburk, the princess lives.

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.050
You don't want to believe otherwise.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:07.030
Apparently she staged her death.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.520
She's a wily one.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.060
She's already arrived at the capital 
and is on her way to this castle.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.550
You have nothing to 
fear, Lord Jugglaburk.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.690
Who are you, again?

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.050
Your minister of state, my Liege.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:27.370
What is the meaning of this?

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:31.480
The Ulga sorority reported that 
they had taken care of the princess.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.200
We must lower our opinion 
of the sorority.

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.380
What shall we do about the princess?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.850
Nothing.

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.930
All I will do is take 
her hand in marriage.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:44.710
It is more important that we put 
that sorority in its place.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:45.380
My lord.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:52.080
Wow!

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:53.740
Don't dilly dally, Kon.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.910
We're going to go to the 
emperor's audience room,

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.190
but I'm not sure we can 
make it before noon.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:02.650
Uh, we just had breakfast.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:05.400
We're going to take the 
cable car up from here.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.460
There's also a pedestrian 
route, but it takes too long.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:09.600
What is this, Mt. Takao?

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.400
Part way through, 
we'll switch to a ropeway.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:13.330
What is this, Hakone?!

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.040
The last part will be going up stairs.

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.250
The north wall will be difficult.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.370
What is this, Eiger?!

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.370
There's also an Alma elevator 
that takes you straight there.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.890
What is this, the Enterprise?!

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.440
Then why don't we just use that?

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.200
Because it's reserved for the elderly.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.800
There really are a lot 
of old people here.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.650
What is this place?

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.320
It's like some creepy old folks' 
home or retirement center.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.050
They are all members of 
the imperial families.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.740
They're the uncles and 
cousins of the princess,

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.830
and all of them have a higher 
claim to the throne than her.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:57.500
So you're saying if all of 
these guys were to croak,

00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:59.330
the princess would be 
quite high on the list?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.570
You're right, they're all 
so old that I want to

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.340
give them something 
for the afterlife.

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.100
All right, enough.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.850
It has been a long time, father.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.740
Who were you again?

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.510
Huh?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.320
Ecarlate, is that you?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.590
I've been hearing that 
name a lot today.

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:28.110
It's been a while.

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:30.680
The old guy's totally off his rocker!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:31.500
Shut up.

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.870
And what are you here for today?

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.130
I have come to collect the 
token of my betrothal.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:38.870
Whose now?

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.170
Mine.

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:44.140
What about breakfast?

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:45.350
I ate before I came.

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.630
But did I have breakfast?

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.650
I told you.

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.130
Be quiet.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:52.870
Here it is.

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:55.890
Did I eat?

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:57.640
Then I will give it to her.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:05.650
All right, then.

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.670
What do you mean, "all right, then"?

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.610
You haven't see your father 
in ages and that's it?

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.710
And what about my situation?

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.660
Looks like talking to this old dude 
isn't going to achieve anything.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.140
Father, it appears that this 
man here is a Hyperion.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:24.160
Hyperion?

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.980
Sure, sure.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:27.670
No way!

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:31.460
He fell from the sky, but he 
doesn't know how to go back.

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.930
Would you happen to know 
how to get to Olvidia?

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:37.430
Olvidia, you say?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:40.870
Well, Olvidia or more like Mitaka...

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:43.230
If I can get back, anywhere 
in the Kanto region would do.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.940
Preferably not further than a 30 
minute walk away from a station.

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.890
If it's matters of the sky, 
you best consult the astrologist.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.950
You can find him at the Western Tower.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:54.950
Though I can see it, as well.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.760
Your destiny, stranger.

00:07:57.950 --> 00:07:59.360
Hyperion?

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.120
No, that's not it.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.710
Your destiny is to...

00:08:08.870 --> 00:08:10.490
Speaking of destiny...

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.390
Oh, I soiled myself.

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:15.290
This way, my liege.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.200
Just a minute!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.490
What about my destiny?!

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:21.140
I'd really like to know, 
if you don't mind!

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:24.320
Who is he again?

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:25.350
Let's go, Kon.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.140
My father is tired.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:28.410
Come on!

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:30.860
Just ask the astrologist 
at the Western Tower!

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.070
This is starting to sound 
like a crappy RPG!

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:36.670
Just keep going from spot to 
spot on a wild goose chase!

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:37.870
Ecarlate...

00:08:40.130 --> 00:08:43.040
I am sorry, but this is for 
the sake of the empire.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.040
Yes.

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:48.230
Who are you again?

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:50.300
Your minister of state, my liege.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.300
So now what do we do?

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.530
We have the token of betrothal,

00:08:57.530 --> 00:09:00.000
so we can make our way to the 
princess's fiancé, Lord Jugglaburk.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:01.310
Where is that?

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.520
Her betrothed's dominion.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.810
Looks like we're going 
on another journey.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:08.110
It will take a few days to 
get the supplies ready.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.070
Until then, we can take a little break.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:13.060
Then I'll go to the Western Tower.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.150
I just hope that astrologist 
isn't doing something weird.

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:17.150
Take care.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.810
So, where is this tower 
in the west, anyway?

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:20.850
Who knows?

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:22.930
I'd never heard of it before, either.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.580
I know west is that way.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.560
There are many towers, though.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.380
I know you guys don't have GPS 
here, so just give me a map.

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:36.050
There should be a library 
two levels below this.

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.350
A library room, huh? Got it.

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:41.730
Wait a minute. I can't 
read your guys' writing.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:43.330
Will someone come with me?

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.800
We haven't been to the 
capital in a long time,

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:46.060
so we've got a lot of 
things to get done.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:48.430
There's a librarian 
there who can help you.

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:49.890
Fine.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.020
So, uh...

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.890
Once I figure out the way,

00:09:55.890 --> 00:09:58.570
I'm just going to go back 
to my world. Is that okay?

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:00.990
I see.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:02.700
Oh, yeah.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.070
That's fine.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.750
There won't be any danger from here.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:08.880
I'll come back to say goodbye.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:15.690
I guess we'll be saying bye to Kon, too.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.260
That's too bad.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.690
That was the deal.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:24.430
I'm lost!

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.900
That's too soon!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.000
Where is the library?

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.470
In general, where the hell is this?

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:30.520
What direction did I come from?

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.780
I don't know!

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.780
Hello? Is there anybody there?

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:38.750
Princess?

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:39.940
Sainglain?

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:40.780
Marian?

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:44.790
I know you're just hiding, 
so come on out!

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:46.430
This is bad.

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.180
I don't have food, I don't have water,

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.860
I don't have a snack, and now I'm 
totally lost and all by my lonesome!

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:51.820
Times like this you find a river 
and start walking downstream

00:10:51.820 --> 00:10:53.790
until you encounter human 
habitation, but there is no river!

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:55.490
This way!

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:00.560
A dead end already?

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.190
That's right, that's right!

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:04.300
Yeah, turn all the capital into cash.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.560
Oh yeah, don't sell 
the jewels just yet.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.010
I heard that their value 
is still going up.

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.370
All right, I'm counting on you.

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:12.680
What are you doing here?

00:11:14.100 --> 00:11:15.850
Brokers are no good these days.

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:17.720
A little slow on the uptake.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:20.820
What are you talking about?

00:11:21.170 --> 00:11:22.940
Just a side job.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:24.830
Earning myself some 
spending money, you see.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:29.330
I'll ignore that part, but what the 
hell are you doing here anyway?

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:32.120
I should ask you the same!

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:35.200
This is the capital's underground, 
its so called Dark Zone,

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:36.830
a place for secret 
wheelings and dealings,

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:39.090
so it makes perfect sense
 for me to be here.

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.090
Does it now?

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:43.560
Shouldn't you be more 
worried about yourself?

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:46.170
I've heard that all sorts 
of dangerous crooks

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.350
are making their moves
 in the capital lately.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.850
I... I... Well, if I'm perfectly 
honest, I'm here because I'm lost.

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.050
Then I wish you all the luck.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:55.540
Hey, now hang on just a minute!

00:11:55.540 --> 00:11:58.400
Hay is for horses.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:01.150
I guess I need to be nicer 
if I want a favor from you.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.110
I keep forgetting since you 
look like a little beast.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:06.690
Well, what is it that 
you came here to do?

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:08.620
Don't tell me you forgot that, as well.

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:11.260
I came to look for the Western Tower,

00:12:11.260 --> 00:12:12.510
so I could speak to the astrologist.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:16.450
Well, once a man has determined his 
goal, he's got to see it to the end.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.100
I'll lend you a hand.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.240
You know how to get 
to the Western Tower?

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.050
I roughly know which 
direction is west, yes.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.200
Why don't you go that way and then 
start looking for the astrologist?

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:25.890
Will you help me?

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:26.970
All right.

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:30.450
But just so you know, 
my route goes underground.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:32.460
It's not without danger.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.870
Danger is my middle name!

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.900
Sounds like we're on 
the same wavelength.

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:42.690
Careful, careful!

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:44.070
If we fall, there's no reset.

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:44.910
What is this, <i>Ico</i>?

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:49.780
Run, before it closes!

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:50.760
What is this,<i> Zelda</i>?!

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:57.880
If you slip even a little, you die.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.420
What is this, <i>Spelunker</i>?!

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:03.250
What is this, <i>Dig Dug</i>?!

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.680
What's that?

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:09.650
An illegal gathering.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.850
Not a rare occurrence, 
here in the underground.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:12.600
Here.

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:15.550
You can't afford to let an underground 
organization see your face.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:25.810
The empire is in a hopeless position.

00:13:25.810 --> 00:13:27.940
There is no hope for reformation now.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:29.160
Yeah!

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:30.970
What kind of gathering is this?

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.160
A gathering of those who 
want to overthrow the empire.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:35.160
Who's there?!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:37.980
Dogs of the empire!

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.270
Or should I say rats?

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:41.050
Have you come here to 
spy on our secrets?

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.670
Just passing through!

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:45.170
Fine, you can take our secrets 
to the afterlife, so listen up!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:47.180
No thank you!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:50.330
Just as you guessed, we are the AEP.

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:51.830
We are the Anti-Empire People who will

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.180
purge the land of this 
antiquated system!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:54.430
Please don't tell me who you are!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.960
Now that you know who we are, 
consider your lives forfeit.

00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:58.810
I knew it!

00:13:58.810 --> 00:13:59.810
You're not getting away!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:03.250
I saw an anti-empire organization's 
rally in the capital, they're sure to kill me!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:04.770
At this rate, I'm going to get killed!

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.620
Give us freedom!

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:10.530
The love for small animals 
is equal for all!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.770
We want to love small animals, as well!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.080
Yeah!

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.830
Give us freedom!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.530
Kittens and muscles!

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:21.340
Puppies and muscles!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.590
And baby pandas!

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.840
And baby koalas!

00:14:24.280 --> 00:14:26.050
What is this now?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:27.680
Some reform group, I guess.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:29.640
Who's there?!

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.460
Dogs of the empire!

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:33.890
Or should I say rats?

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:35.680
Have you come here to 
spy on our secrets?

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.350
Just passing through!

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:41.300
Fine, you can take our secrets 
to the afterlife, so listen up!

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:42.520
No thank you!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:46.510
Just as you guessed, we are the AEM&P!

00:14:46.510 --> 00:14:48.270
We shall bring new 
freedom to the empire,

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:51.760
we are Anti-Empire Muscles & Pets!

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.540
I don't really get your goals...

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:57.770
I won't let you stand in our way!

00:14:57.770 --> 00:14:59.210
I won't stand in your way!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:14:59.870
You're not getting away!

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.380
I already have two secrets 
for the afterlife already.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:03.470
Not that I want any!

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:04.800
I mean secrets about maids could

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.430
maybe be nice, but not that kind!

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:07.980
We want rights!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:10.590
What now?

00:15:10.770 --> 00:15:12.630
The empire's fashion is outdated!

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:15.030
Why can't we just wear what we want?!

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:18.220
We want our rights!

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.940
Is it weird for men to cross-dress?!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.000
It isn't!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.930
Do frills and beards not go together?!

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:27.830
They're fine together!

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.520
What kind of group is this?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.850
Who knows?

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.100
Who is there?!

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.890
Dogs of the empire, I'm sure.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.360
Or should I say rats?

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.510
Have you come here to 
spy on our secrets?

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.080
Just passing through!

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:44.080
Fine, you can take our secrets 
to the afterlife, so listen up!

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:47.580
You can take our secrets to 
the afterlife, so listen up!

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:48.840
No thank you!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.980
Just as you guessed, we are the AEG!

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.960
We shall bring new fashion 
to the outdated empire,

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.350
we are the Anti-Empire Girls!

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.140
Shouldn't the G stand for 
guys instead of girls?

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.510
I'm so mad!

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.100
I'm a girl at heart!

00:16:02.500 --> 00:16:06.140
You dare expose our true 
identities?! I won't forgive you!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:11.780
You're not getting away!

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:13.990
Hurry, go straight!

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:23.690
You're not getting away.

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.840
That's my prey!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.300
Tiger Muscle?!

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:32.800
It's been a while, Mr. Z.

00:16:33.200 --> 00:16:35.300
What, you know each other?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.690
I had assumed you had died.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:40.310
I just left the 
capital for a spell.

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:44.310
I can't die until the empire's 
way of thinking has been changed.

00:16:44.510 --> 00:16:46.430
The empire will split up soon.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.710
No, the empire will 
accept the New Fashion!

00:16:52.470 --> 00:16:54.070
Je T'Aime's Star?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.650
Oh, you, too?

00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:59.330
It looks like we have to 
settle our score tonight.

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:03.160
Huh? What's going on now?

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.290
It looks like these three 
have some history.

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:08.340
You'll have your chance while 
they have their battle.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:10.250
Taste my sword of justice!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.080
Power is not justice! 
Muscles are justice!

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:14.840
I won't let you defile 
the word justice!

00:17:17.650 --> 00:17:18.470
Now, Kon!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.770
You scoundrels disturbing the 
capital, I shall vanquish you!

00:17:30.670 --> 00:17:32.780
I am Captain Empire!

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:34.470
A newcomer!

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:36.510
Another weirdo.

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:38.630
You're one to talk!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:42.290
Freedom to cosplay! I'm Slayer Z!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.360
Down with rules! I'm Cosmic Comic!

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.790
Allow our events! I'm Big Banzai!

00:17:48.090 --> 00:17:50.440
Looks like the capital has 
gotten quite diverse.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.050
It looks like there is no other 
way than to split it up.

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.300
I'll take you all on!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.770
Muscles and kittens!

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.140
Free fashion!

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.640
Revolution!

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:08.250
I can't, no more...

00:18:08.250 --> 00:18:10.460
We're almost there. 
Pull yourself together!

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:12.060
That's the astrologist's tower.

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:27.100
Excuse me for disturbing 
you so late at night.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.280
Is anybody here?

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:31.980
I don't care that I simply came in,

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.320
but since I can't get any 
information otherwise,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:36.750
I'm asking like this...

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:38.840
Who's there?

00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:45.180
Are you the astrologist?

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:46.590
Yes.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:49.550
Could you tell me how 
to get to Olvidia?

00:18:49.550 --> 00:18:50.950
Nope.

00:18:50.950 --> 00:18:51.870
Huh?

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.860
That's something you'd have 
to ask an Alma technician.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:57.360
I can tell you your fortune 
for tomorrow, though.

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.620
Damn it! I knew that 
emperor was useless.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.390
Jugglaburk.

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.120
Was that...

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:06.120
Strange, nobody should be up there.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.660
Go to Jugglaburk's domain.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:09.870
This voice...

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:11.270
Hey!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.090
Go to Jugglaburk's domain.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:21.080
The key to your return is there.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:24.700
Um, could you be a 
little more specific?

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.910
Actually, who are you?

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:27.670
Go to Jugglaburk's domain.

00:19:27.670 --> 00:19:30.140
Argh, she repeated her line already!

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.650
So what, I can't get any additional 
information in this area?

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:34.900
Other than by rifling through dressers?

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:37.900
I think all that's left is to go home.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:40.450
I'm sick of this cheap 
role-playing crap!

00:19:42.510 --> 00:19:43.160
Huh?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:56.340
Is that the Comet Empire?

00:19:56.660 --> 00:19:59.000
That's the floating city Olvidia.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.280
You will eventually make it to Olvidia.

00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:06.970
To reach it, go to 
Jugglaburk's domain.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:32.860
Who are they?

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:34.200
They're strong!

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:35.880
The imperial guard is here!

00:20:36.140 --> 00:20:37.310
Arrest them!

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:38.880
The military police is here, too!

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.190
Arrest them!

00:20:40.190 --> 00:20:41.880
The rifle unit is here, too!

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.350
Muskets!

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.890
Run!

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:49.450
Looks like this is it.

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:52.520
I thought we were going to settle this.

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:57.450
We are still fickle creatures who 
have to hide in the shadows.

00:20:58.010 --> 00:21:00.200
Like she said. We shall meet again.

00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:04.120
When the morning comes, I disappear...

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:06.080
Je je je t'aime!

00:21:13.680 --> 00:21:15.920
Um, good morning.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:19.230
What is it? Did you 
come to say goodbye?

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:24.090
Actually, I'm also going 
to Jugglaburk's domain.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:25.730
I see, and?

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:29.180
Well, can't I come with you?

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:33.430
If you're going continue to be 
my servant, I have no issues.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.460
We don't have to change 
anything, so thanks.

00:21:35.930 --> 00:21:37.690
Where are Sainglain and Marian?

00:21:38.390 --> 00:21:40.760
They're both strangely 
late this morning.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:44.700
I'm sorry, I overslept!

00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:49.300
I had a really hard time 
getting up this morning.

00:21:50.790 --> 00:21:51.800
Oh, Kon.

00:21:51.800 --> 00:21:53.210
You're back?

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:53.950
Yeah.

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:56.560
Come in.

00:21:58.710 --> 00:21:59.710
Excuse me.

00:22:00.740 --> 00:22:02.710
Lord Nabokov sent me.

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:06.220
Huh?

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.510
And what do you want?

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:16.080
Lord Jugglaburk has offered 
to take you to his domain.

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:22.690
That's an airship! 
So they have them here, too.

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:25.200
It's a sky boat. It'll be 
just a quick trip with this.

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:29.410
That is Lord Nabokov 
Jugglaburk over there.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:24.900
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:14.220
For our failure to prevent Princess 
Ecarlate from entering the capital,

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:17.600
we, Incognito, have been ordered to 
stand by until we receive new orders.

00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:22.030
However, I can't just sit idly by and 
watch them make it to Jugglaburk's domain.

00:24:22.030 --> 00:24:24.480
I've snuck onto the sky boat by myself.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:30.600
As the wedding actually becomes 
tangible for the princess,

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:30.600
Kon and the others don't 
know how to feel.

00:24:30.600 --> 00:24:34.700
However, then the shadow of a 
cold-blooded killer creeps closer.

00:24:30.600 --> 00:24:34.700
Watch out! Run!
